00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:31.760
It's so good.

1070
00:34:31.760 --> 00:34:32.560
It's so relatable.

1071
00:34:32.920 --> 00:34:32.970
Yeah.

1072
00:34:32.970 --> 00:34:34.420
And the performances are just amazing.

1073
00:34:34.420 --> 00:34:35.180
That's amazing.

1074
00:34:35.600 --> 00:34:35.760
Yeah.

1075
00:34:35.900 --> 00:34:36.040
Yeah.

1076
00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:39.880
And I feel like you guys change television, you know, because you just brought everything

1077
00:34:39.880 --> 00:34:41.160
down a notch.

1078
00:34:41.660 --> 00:34:45.200
Still, like I said, still managing to pull off big laughs, giant set pieces.

1079
00:34:45.560 --> 00:34:50.100
But man, it's just so nice to see people behaving like people, you know, and like when we go

1080
00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:54.640
back and watch our show, as much as I'm able to say, like, it was good, like it was, you

1081
00:34:54.640 --> 00:34:59.620
know, it's a sitcom, you know, it's a very stylized form of rhythm and acting and it has

1082
00:34:59.620 --> 00:35:00.420
its benefits.

1083
00:35:01.020 --> 00:35:05.860
Realism though, like, you know, I mean, often we would have moments of realism, but you know,

1084
00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:10.540
the jokes were like, you know, you're just hitting it and you guys didn't have any of

1085
00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:13.500
that still had a musicality, still had a rhythm, but it was part of the camera.

1086
00:35:13.820 --> 00:35:15.080
It's really remarkable.

1087
00:35:15.200 --> 00:35:16.080
And yeah.

1088
00:35:16.300 --> 00:35:21.780
But what you were doing is really difficult and you do it so well on the show and I couldn't

