This is in my wheelhouse.

1121
00:36:12.340 --> 00:36:14.620
I just spent nine years being the bitchy principal.

1122
00:36:14.760 --> 00:36:14.940
Right.

1123
00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:19.940
And I said the line and the director was like, louder, say it louder.

1124
00:36:20.320 --> 00:36:23.200
And then I said it louder, but then it sounded weird.

1125
00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:28.160
And then he was like, can we get her like maybe a cane, like a cane, like she comes in

1126
00:36:28.160 --> 00:36:32.020
like with a, like a, and I was like, and he goes, maybe she has a hat.

1127
00:36:32.360 --> 00:36:36.940
And Craig Ferguson was in the episode with me and we had become friends at this point.

1128
00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:39.700
And he goes, maybe we get her a parrot and a parrot.

1129
00:36:39.700 --> 00:36:40.240
Yeah, exactly.

1130
00:36:41.920 --> 00:36:42.620
There you go.

1131
00:36:42.760 --> 00:36:44.080
But they were trying to sitcom it up.

1132
00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:48.720
They were trying to like make me more of a, a bigger character.

1133
00:36:48.940 --> 00:36:50.100
And I, I'd forgotten.

1134
00:36:50.320 --> 00:36:51.320
I didn't know how to do it.

1135
00:36:51.580 --> 00:36:55.540
Probably you'd gotten so used to the volume and tone level that you guys were on.

1136
00:36:55.660 --> 00:36:56.400
It's so different.

1137
00:36:56.620 --> 00:37:01.080
And I do love sketch comedy, but I think like, I didn't know how to time it out with all

1138
00:37:01.080 --> 00:37:01.940
the moving parts.

1139
00:37:01.940 --> 00:37:07.580
Well, just thank God the office came along for me because I did not thrive in the three

1140
00:37:07.580 --> 00:37:08.220
camera world.

1141
00:37:08.320 --> 00:37:09.640
I really tried.

1142
00:37:09.740 --> 00:37:15.420
I always thought that I was like a pretty naturally funny person and that comedy was my thing in

1143
00:37:15.420 --> 00:37:19.820
terms of comedy acting, but I was not a fit for the three camera style.

1144
00:37:20.180 --> 00:37:26.760
In fact, the one major role that I landed was the pilot of, um, man with a plan starring

1145
00:37:26.760 --> 00:37:27.540
Matt LeBlanc.

1146
00:37:27.660 --> 00:37:31.100
I was on for many, many seasons without me.

1147
00:37:31.940 --> 00:37:32.680
That was fire.

1148
00:37:32.960 --> 00:37:33.580
Guys are the pilot.

1149
00:37:34.240 --> 00:37:34.680
Yeah.

1150
00:37:35.120 --> 00:37:35.240
Yeah.

1151
00:37:35.240 --> 00:37:38.560
That was my big job after the office was man with a plan.

1152
00:37:38.720 --> 00:37:39.960
And I just struggled.

1153
00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:42.100
I was like, why can't I do this?

1154
00:37:42.260 --> 00:37:43.360
It is not easy.

1155
00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:46.020
And I really respect anyone who can do it.

1156
00:37:46.160 --> 00:37:46.400
Yeah.

1157
00:37:46.600 --> 00:37:49.480
You both thrive on the office.

1158
00:37:49.540 --> 00:37:50.100
It's amazing.

1159
00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:53.840
Well, I wanted to say that I think one of the reasons why the office was so successful

1160
00:37:53.840 --> 00:37:58.260
is not just you would arguably be in the conversation for best ensemble cast on TV and mainstream

1161
00:37:58.260 --> 00:37:58.660
TV.

1162
00:37:58.780 --> 00:37:59.320
Yeah, that's true.

1163
00:37:59.320 --> 00:38:02.400
But there's so much heart that's unexpected.

1164
00:38:02.640 --> 00:38:07.280
I remember watching an interview with your editor who said that as he was editing the

1165
00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:12.000
scene where Jim and Pam are on the boat for the booze cruise that he's editing, he goes,

1166
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:13.500
I knew what happened.

1167
00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:15.480
And I was still there going, kiss her.

1168
00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:16.340
Kiss her.

1169
00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:17.340
Come on, Jim.

1170
00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:17.860
Kiss her.

1171
00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:19.340
You're working on the show.

1172
00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:20.920
You know what's going to happen.

1173
00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:24.880
And you're still so invested that you're yelling at the screen to have the characters kiss.

1174
00:38:24.880 --> 00:38:29.840
That's rare in any medium, but on television at the time, it was unheard of.

1175
00:38:30.020 --> 00:38:33.040
So we were yelling at the screen, things like that.

1176
00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:33.540
Kiss her.

1177
00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:34.300
And oh, my God.

1178
00:38:34.520 --> 00:38:36.880
And Jim can't come back from Stanford with her.

1179
00:38:37.080 --> 00:38:37.320
Come on.

1180
00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:38.420
And Pam's doing this.

1181
00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:41.100
When she walks across the hot coals, we were just invested in everything.

1182
00:38:41.380 --> 00:38:43.660
And then on top of that, it was hysterical.

1183
00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:47.320
So that was just an added bonus to the show was lightning in a bottle.

1184
00:38:47.460 --> 00:38:49.560
I mean, it's tough to get that again.

1185
00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:50.940
I don't know if we ever will, frankly.

1186
00:38:50.940 --> 00:38:55.700
I mean, I don't know if I ever will, you know, it was it was a dream job.

1187
00:38:55.900 --> 00:38:58.480
They came around at the exact right time.

1188
00:38:58.880 --> 00:39:00.500
And I felt like I was ready.

1189
00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:06.760
My acting coach always says successful come when your readiness meets the opportunities.

1190
00:39:06.940 --> 00:39:11.180
And so you can be as ready as you are and then never have an opportunity.

1191
00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:13.800
But likewise, you can have all the opportunities in the world,

1192
00:39:13.980 --> 00:39:17.120
which I was getting with all of my auditions for three camera shows.

1193
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:18.720
But I wasn't ready.

1194
00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:24.460
And so the office for me was the thing where finally the opportunity met the readiness.

1195
00:39:24.780 --> 00:39:26.760
I think that's true for a lot of our cast, too,

1196
00:39:26.880 --> 00:39:31.080
because we had a lot of really great seasoned comedians that had just been,

1197
00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.460
you know, plugging away.

1198
00:39:32.680 --> 00:39:34.180
Kate Flannery is hilarious.

1199
00:39:34.480 --> 00:39:37.740
She was part of a lounge act called The Lampshades.

1200
00:39:37.980 --> 00:39:39.900
Oscar Nunez, I had met at the Groundlings.

1201
00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:41.280
He was in Hot Towel.

1202
00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:43.600
We had a scene together.

1203
00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:47.620
You know, obviously, Steve, Rain, everyone had been sort of putting their dues in,

1204
00:39:47.720 --> 00:39:49.840
putting their time in, and it was just that right moment.

1205
00:39:50.060 --> 00:39:51.460
But I have a question for you guys.

1206
00:39:51.860 --> 00:39:57.560
So, OK, if you could play a character on The Office, like, which one would you want to play?

1207
00:39:57.720 --> 00:39:58.960
Oh, that's such a good question.

1208
