At the end of this six episodes, those first six, they printed my name on paper,

1243
00:41:08.760 --> 00:41:12.140
and they just laminated it with some Velcro, and that's what was on my door.

1244
00:41:12.540 --> 00:41:15.560
So I took my laminated piece of paper home with me.

1245
00:41:15.960 --> 00:41:16.380
Yeah.

1246
00:41:17.900 --> 00:41:19.040
I'll save it forever.

1247
00:41:19.600 --> 00:41:21.040
Because we just thought that was it.

1248
00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:21.460
That was it.

1249
00:41:21.460 --> 00:41:26.940
So what episode would you then look to and say, that's the one where we knew what we were doing.

1250
00:41:27.080 --> 00:41:29.000
Everybody knew we were going to go from here.

1251
00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:30.020
We're now a hit.

1252
00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:30.960
This is what's going to happen.

1253
00:41:31.180 --> 00:41:37.500
It's very clear to me as far as like the downloads, because the Christmas episode with Yankee Swap

1254
00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:42.920
and Baby's playing jazz poster and Phyllis' sad oven mitt, all of that, the teapot,

1255
00:41:43.380 --> 00:41:45.940
that episode became the number one download on iTunes.

1256
00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:46.480
Okay.

1257
00:41:46.920 --> 00:41:47.300
And so...

1258
00:41:47.780 --> 00:41:49.040
The ratings weren't there.

1259
00:41:49.180 --> 00:41:50.280
The ratings weren't there.

1260
00:41:50.600 --> 00:41:56.660
But this new world of like, oh, wait, we can make money off of this other thing,

1261
00:41:56.920 --> 00:41:58.620
this downloadable item.

1262
00:41:58.620 --> 00:41:59.700
Not the caSt.

1263
00:41:59.900 --> 00:42:00.060
Right.

1264
00:42:00.220 --> 00:42:01.360
The cast doesn't get money for that.

1265
00:42:01.460 --> 00:42:01.800
Right, right.

1266
00:42:01.980 --> 00:42:04.600
But people were watching it on their iPods, remember?

1267
00:42:04.920 --> 00:42:05.440
Like, yes.

1268
00:42:05.840 --> 00:42:06.620
And they were like, okay.

1269
00:42:06.620 --> 00:42:07.500
Also for the Yankee Swap.

1270
00:42:07.580 --> 00:42:07.700
Yes.

1271
00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:08.340
There you go.

1272
00:42:08.460 --> 00:42:08.900
There you go.

1273
00:42:08.980 --> 00:42:09.460
Video iPod.

1274
00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:10.660
Now, what about you guys?

1275
00:42:10.860 --> 00:42:11.980
Did you always have...

1276
00:42:11.980 --> 00:42:15.700
Well, you mentioned individually you felt like you could be fired at any moment, but what

1277
00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:16.800
about the show as a whole?

1278
00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:18.800
Yeah, we always felt like we were pretty much on the bubble.

1279
00:42:18.820 --> 00:42:20.080
We never, ever...

1280
00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:21.380
Maybe three to four or four to five.

1281
00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:23.460
Maybe one season we knew were picked up for the next one.

1282
00:42:23.540 --> 00:42:24.140
Maybe we were kind of...

1283
00:42:24.140 --> 00:42:26.640
It was also just a weird position to be a kid's show.

1284
00:42:26.940 --> 00:42:28.460
We felt like nobody was watching.

1285
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:31.340
You know, like, we'd had no cultural feedback.

1286
00:42:31.700 --> 00:42:31.920
Yeah.

1287
00:42:31.920 --> 00:42:32.760
Like, there was no...

1288
00:42:32.760 --> 00:42:33.820
There was no online culture.

1289
00:42:34.160 --> 00:42:34.220
Right.

1290
00:42:34.300 --> 00:42:36.640
But there was also just no way that kids could...

1291
00:42:36.640 --> 00:42:39.240
Like, we would get recognized, like, couldn't go to the mall.

1292
00:42:39.380 --> 00:42:39.500
Yeah.

1293
00:42:39.620 --> 00:42:43.380
But otherwise, like, as far as, like, the industry, we were nothing.

1294
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:45.580
We felt like we were getting no...

1295
00:42:45.580 --> 00:42:48.640
You know, and so it's only now that we're like, oh my God, we were big.

1296
00:42:48.700 --> 00:42:51.900
Well, we also had one of our other executive producers on, not the one who used to give

1297
00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:55.220
us notes, but another one who just recently came on and said, that was also a network

1298
00:42:55.220 --> 00:42:58.340
thing where they specifically didn't want you to know that you were

1299
00:42:58.340 --> 00:43:02.360
popular so that they couldn't go and ask for more money to make more, make the show.

1300
00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:02.530
Right.

1301
00:43:02.530 --> 00:43:03.940
They wanted us to feel like we were lucky to be there.

1302
00:43:03.940 --> 00:43:06.800
So they would, if you're always on the bubble, then you're lucky we're giving you this budget.

1303
00:43:07.160 --> 00:43:10.220
Like, so don't ask for any more because you barely got picked up.

1304
00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:14.680
Where if we knew the show was, or they knew that the show was popular, the executive producers

1305
00:43:14.680 --> 00:43:15.940
go in and ask for the moon.

1306
00:43:15.940 --> 00:43:19.960
And so to stop that, they would kind of make us seem like we're just, we're lucky to be

1307
00:43:19.960 --> 00:43:20.080
there.

1308
00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:21.120
Don't forget you're lucky to be there.

1309
00:43:21.260 --> 00:43:24.420
Also, we were canceled in 2000 with what, like a 25 share?

1310
00:43:24.680 --> 00:43:25.080
Yeah, right.

1311
00:43:25.240 --> 00:43:28.900
And like, you know, nowadays, everybody would chill for that kind of audience.

1312
00:43:28.900 --> 00:43:29.120
Yeah, yes.

1313
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:30.660
But that was a big drop for us.

1314
00:43:30.880 --> 00:43:33.200
So that was, I mean, it was like, oh my God, we're only getting a 25.

1315
00:43:33.460 --> 00:43:33.820
Yeah, we're done.

1316
00:43:33.820 --> 00:43:37.320
Did you feel like you got to wrap up the show?

1317
00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:38.520
Yeah, yeah.

1318
00:43:38.720 --> 00:43:38.860
Definitely.

1319
00:43:38.860 --> 00:43:43.780
We got a nice, you know, we had a very nice hour long with the retrospective and where

1320
00:43:43.780 --> 00:43:44.420
everybody moves.

1321
00:43:44.480 --> 00:43:46.240
We really did get a chance to say goodbye.

1322
00:43:46.420 --> 00:43:47.280
It wasn't like we were just done.

1323
00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:48.600
And our final scene was so great.

1324
00:43:48.840 --> 00:43:50.460
It was a really nice final scene.

1325
00:43:50.540 --> 00:43:51.580
And we were all like really crying.

1326
00:43:51.840 --> 00:43:52.640
Actually, in the classroom.

1327
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:54.040
We didn't rehearse it throughout the week.

1328
00:43:54.140 --> 00:43:57.500
We just read it at table read and then shot it once in front of the audience.

1329
00:43:57.660 --> 00:43:58.060
That was it.

1330
00:43:58.080 --> 00:44:03.600
And so it's us saying goodbye to Bill Daniels as Mr. Feeney and all of us just real emotion.

1331
00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:06.820
Brian kind of talking to each other in character.

1332
00:44:07.340 --> 00:44:08.100
Very emotional.

1333
00:44:08.300 --> 00:44:08.700
Wow.

1334
00:44:08.880 --> 00:44:10.220
I'm very thankful for that.

1335
00:44:10.280 --> 00:44:13.420
And I don't think a lot of, you know, actors get that experience.

1336
00:44:13.600 --> 00:44:15.100
It's just you're just done.

1337
00:44:15.300 --> 00:44:17.040
You don't get any like notice.

1338
00:44:17.260 --> 00:44:18.740
But yeah, your character doesn't get closure.

1339
00:44:18.940 --> 00:44:21.120
You don't get closure as a group or as a crew.

1340
00:44:21.440 --> 00:44:23.560
A lot of people just get canceled.

1341
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:25.200
You're just like, not next year, guys.

1342
00:44:25.380 --> 00:44:26.080
You're like, oh.

1343
00:44:26.520 --> 00:44:30.100
For me, moving into any other acting job after Boy Meets World was a shock.

1344
00:44:30.240 --> 00:44:31.700
It was like, wait, we're not all best friends.

1345
00:44:31.700 --> 00:44:33.160
We're going to be together forever.

1346
00:44:33.160 --> 00:44:34.600
You're like, oh, right.

1347
00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:36.340
That is such a rare gift.

1348
00:44:36.640 --> 00:44:36.780
Yeah.

1349
00:44:37.260 --> 00:44:41.520
Well, I was going to say that I think that's something that our casts have in common, which

1350
00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:45.840
is that, like Angela was saying, for a lot of the people in the office, this was really

1351
00:44:45.840 --> 00:44:47.400
our first big job.

1352
00:44:47.660 --> 00:44:47.880
Yeah.

1353
00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:51.680
And you're a very open vessel when it's your first big job.

1354
00:44:51.700 --> 00:44:54.200
And we all like learned together.

1355
00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:56.780
We learned about parts of the industry together.

1356
00:44:57.040 --> 00:44:58.960
Like none of us had ever done a junket.

1357
00:44:59.380 --> 00:45:01.380
None of us had ever been to the upfront.

1358
00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:06.260
So to all the like business stuff that goes behind the making of a show or the publicity

1359
00:45:06.260 --> 00:45:06.860
or anything.

1360
00:45:06.860 --> 00:45:10.740
And so we're really bonded, not just because of the show we were on, but because we kind

1361
00:45:10.740 --> 00:45:13.160
of learned about the entertainment business together.

1362
00:45:13.400 --> 00:45:13.820
Satellite Mediator.

1363
00:45:14.160 --> 00:45:14.420
Yeah.

1364
00:45:15.160 --> 00:45:16.200
Get up at 4 a.m.

1365
00:45:16.360 --> 00:45:17.900
and talk to 25 news stations.

1366
00:45:18.320 --> 00:45:19.540
25 radio stations.

1367
00:45:19.940 --> 00:45:20.700
That have a delay.

1368
00:45:20.880 --> 00:45:21.940
But you can't see them.

1369
00:45:21.940 --> 00:45:22.820
You can't sit there like.

1370
00:45:23.340 --> 00:45:23.700
Yeah.

1371
00:45:23.700 --> 00:45:24.780
You can't see them at night.

1372
00:45:24.860 --> 00:45:25.120
Yeah.

1373
00:45:25.220 --> 00:45:25.500
Yeah.

1374
00:45:25.720 --> 00:45:25.780
Exactly.

1375
00:45:26.640 --> 00:45:27.140
I'm sorry.

1376
00:45:27.360 --> 00:45:28.100
You go ahead.

1377
00:45:28.840 --> 00:45:31.860
And also, you guys must have been there for each other for just fame.

1378
00:45:32.100 --> 00:45:34.840
Like what that weird experience is like of like getting recognized.

1379
00:45:34.840 --> 00:45:35.880
And now everybody's talking.

1380
00:45:36.020 --> 00:45:38.880
It's like a weird thing, you know, and we're so glad we had each other.

1381
00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:39.220
Like.

1382
00:45:39.360 --> 00:45:39.500
Yeah.

1383
00:45:39.560 --> 00:45:43.300
We have people come up and say this to us all the time, which is like, you look like

1384
00:45:43.300 --> 00:45:45.160
an older version of that lady on the office.

1385
00:45:45.600 --> 00:45:46.060
Oh, my God.

1386
00:45:46.100 --> 00:45:47.760
And people in PR are like, that's true.

1387
00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:49.180
You are correct.

1388
00:45:49.980 --> 00:45:50.620
We are.

1389
00:45:50.620 --> 00:45:50.820
We are.

1390
00:45:51.080 --> 00:45:51.760
We are.

1391
00:45:52.100 --> 00:45:52.150
We are.

1392
00:45:52.150 --> 00:45:52.200
We are.

1393
00:45:52.200 --> 00:45:52.300
We are.

1394
00:45:52.300 --> 00:45:52.440
We are.

1395
00:45:53.540 --> 00:45:54.300
I know.

1396
00:45:55.480 --> 00:45:59.340
Hindsight being what it is, would you have had done anything else with your characters

1397
00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:01.740
or anything different with your characters if you could go back and do it again?

1398
00:46:01.860 --> 00:46:02.340
You know what?

1399
00:46:02.520 --> 00:46:02.920
Yes.

1400
00:46:04.480 --> 00:46:09.260
I maybe would not have changed Pam's hair.

1401
00:46:09.900 --> 00:46:10.440
Really?

1402
00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:17.120
I kind of fought to change the frizzy mullet when she started dating Jim.

1403
00:46:17.320 --> 00:46:20.200
I said, I think she's growing as a person.

1404
00:46:20.580 --> 00:46:25.880
And I had this whole thing in my head character-wise that she was going to go to art school and she's

1405
00:46:25.880 --> 00:46:27.320
with her love now.

1406
00:46:27.500 --> 00:46:31.960
And so maybe she's going to do more than just, you know, let her hair air dry and put

1407
00:46:31.960 --> 00:46:32.520
it in a clip.

1408
00:46:32.800 --> 00:46:36.120
Like maybe she's just going to primp a little bit more.

1409
00:46:36.280 --> 00:46:41.540
And then later, I became sort of sad that that sort of signature hairdo was gone.

1410
00:46:41.540 --> 00:46:43.440
So you might see it in later seasons.

1411
00:46:43.440 --> 00:46:46.780
I tried to bring it back a tiny bit.

1412
00:46:46.800 --> 00:46:52.300
But when I rewatched the show, I became somewhat sad when Pam's hair changed.

1413
00:46:52.300 --> 00:46:52.640
Okay.

1414
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:53.480
That's so funny.

1415
00:46:53.580 --> 00:46:56.860
And I kind of wish that I had just let her be.

1416
