Some of that was a little bit selfish because what would happen is after work,

1434
00:47:29.920 --> 00:47:32.760
maybe there'd be an event or something we wanted to go to.

1435
00:47:33.120 --> 00:47:33.220
Right.

1436
00:47:33.400 --> 00:47:37.160
And I didn't want to go to that event with frizzy Pam hair.

1437
00:47:37.560 --> 00:47:37.660
Yeah.

1438
00:47:37.940 --> 00:47:41.980
And so I was like, if I could be halfway there, if you could just help me a little bit.

1439
00:47:42.200 --> 00:47:42.400
Yeah.

1440
00:47:42.440 --> 00:47:43.820
It would be a lot easier.

1441
00:47:44.220 --> 00:47:49.600
That's part of the rewatch is like recognizing how different the lived experience is.

1442
00:47:49.700 --> 00:47:53.120
Like the lived experience as an actor is like, I want my hair to look like my hair.

1443
00:47:53.200 --> 00:47:55.100
I don't care about the iconography of Pam.

1444
00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:58.640
But now that you can go back and watch it, you're like, actually, that iconography was pretty great.

1445
00:47:58.640 --> 00:47:59.040
Yeah.

1446
00:47:59.280 --> 00:48:00.060
A hundred percent.

1447
00:48:00.380 --> 00:48:02.060
You can see it more like the way your producer did, right?

1448
00:48:02.140 --> 00:48:03.720
Like you can see you with your hair.

1449
00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:04.560
Oh, yeah.

1450
00:48:04.580 --> 00:48:05.320
It's like, why?

1451
00:48:05.540 --> 00:48:09.700
You know, at the time, you know, it's like your lived experience is really, it's important.

1452
00:48:09.880 --> 00:48:11.820
And as an actor, you know, but a good actor.

1453
00:48:11.820 --> 00:48:14.760
But for us, it was also because of how we grew up on the set.

1454
00:48:14.900 --> 00:48:16.260
It was a little bit of control.

1455
00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:16.680
Oh, yeah.

1456
00:48:16.860 --> 00:48:20.060
Like if we could go and cut our hair, then we had a little bit of control.

1457
00:48:20.480 --> 00:48:20.960
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

1458
00:48:21.040 --> 00:48:21.760
It's a different thing.

1459
00:48:21.900 --> 00:48:25.160
But I think like as an actor, it is hard to recognize, you know, like.

1460
00:48:25.360 --> 00:48:26.140
What about you, Anne?

1461
00:48:26.220 --> 00:48:27.440
I wouldn't change anything.

1462
00:48:27.600 --> 00:48:27.780
Nothing.

1463
00:48:28.640 --> 00:48:29.280
I just, um.

